{"t": 1794108409.8604598, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "checkout \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731)\n\nCause: payment gateway API 2026-11 enforces \"strict amounts\"; `amount` must be an integer in minor units (cents). checkout was sending a decimal EUR value (e.g. 12.34), so the gateway rejected charges with 400 invalid_amount (38% 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC).\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py now converts EUR to integer cents (12.34 -> 1234) using Decimal with half-up rounding; `currency` remains EUR. Verified locally against the gateway's stated contract.\n\nStatus: fix is in the working tree, not yet deployed. No config or data changes needed; alert should clear once checkout is redeployed."}, "ok": true}
